---
/** Present the pilot's accepted evidence without combining process, result, or independent conversations. */
import study from '../../public/agentic-le/dynamic/study/overview.json';
const axes = {human_flourishing: 'Human flourishing support', system_performance: 'System performance', learning: 'Learning'};
const shortCase = (run) => run.run_id.startsWith('handoff') ? 'Handoff' : 'Workshop';
const processReview = (version) => version?.reviews.find(review => review.scope === 'process');
const score = (review, criterion) => !review ? 'Pending' : review.scores.find(item => item.dimension_id === criterion)?.score ?? 'Unknown';
const rows = study.runs.flatMap(run => run.versions.flatMap((version, index) => run.scenarios.map(scenario => ({
  run, version, scenario, stage: index === 0 ? 'Initial' : 'User update',
  review: version.reviews.find(review => review.scope === 'result' && review.scenario_id === scenario.id)
}))));
const updates = study.runs.flatMap(run => run.versions.slice(1).map(version => ({run, version})));
const resultLabels = ['Agency and access', 'Task behavior', 'Recovery', 'Capability support', 'Feedback and revision', 'Credible use'];
const timestamp = new Date(study.updated_at).toLocaleString('en-GB', {timeZone: 'UTC', dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short'}) + ' UTC';
---
<section class="workspace-card pilot-evidence" id="pilot-results" aria-labelledby="pilot-results-title">
  <h2 id="pilot-results-title">New dynamic pilot: recorded evidence</h2>
  <p>Two modest cases, each explored by a specialist team and a generalist: <strong>four independent design conversations, one per case and condition</strong>. Each frozen design receives easy, medium and hard tests. These repeated scenarios are not additional teams or learners.</p>
  <p class="muted">Evidence snapshot: <time datetime={study.updated_at}>{timestamp}</time>. Open a conversation for the complete messages, version history, observed output and quoted reasons behind each rating.</p>
  <div class="evidence-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Initial pilot conversations and completed evidence">
    <table><caption>Initial designs and evidence coverage</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Case and condition</th><th scope="col">Accepted messages</th><th scope="col">Contributing actors</th><th scope="col">Frozen version</th><th scope="col">Test records</th><th scope="col">Expert reviews</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{study.runs.map(run => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={`/agentic-le/dynamic/?run=${run.run_id}`}>{shortCase(run)} · {run.condition}</a></th><td>{run.initial_messages}</td><td>{run.initial_actors}</td><td>{run.versions[0] ? `v${run.versions[0].artifact_version}` : 'Pending'}</td><td>{run.versions[0]?.observations.length ?? 0} / 3</td><td>{run.versions[0]?.reviews.length ?? 0} / 4</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Message and actor counts describe the accepted conversation through its first freeze, including the facilitator. For an unfrozen candidate they show progress so far. Failed attempts remain in the record. Longer conversations and more approvals are not measures of solution quality.</p>
  <details class="disclosure"><summary>Inspect the expert process ratings</summary>
    <p>One separate model expert reviews each frozen version. Scores range from 0 to 4; unknown evidence remains unknown. The evaluator sees the assigned roles and conversation. These are descriptive judgments, with no combined score or condition ranking.</p>
    <div class="evidence-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Initial process criterion ratings"><table><caption>Process ratings for the initial frozen designs</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Criterion</th>{study.runs.map(run => <th scope="col">{shortCase(run)}<br />{run.condition}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{study.rubric.process.map(criterion => <tr><th scope="row">{criterion.label}<small>{axes[criterion.axis]}</small></th>{study.runs.map(run => <td>{score(processReview(run.versions[0]), criterion.id)}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    {updates.map(({run, version}) => <div><h3>{shortCase(run)} · User update · v{version.artifact_version}</h3><dl class="update-scores">{study.rubric.process.map(criterion => <div><dt>{criterion.label}</dt><dd>{score(processReview(version), criterion.id)}</dd></div>)}</dl></div>)}
  </details>
  <details class="disclosure"><summary>Inspect the expert result ratings by scenario</summary>
    <p>These scores concern the actual frozen artifact and observed scenario. Passing browser checks does not establish useful instructional feedback, human learning, or workplace effectiveness. The update uses the same fixtures for regression checking; it is not a fresh holdout test.</p>
    <div class="evidence-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Result ratings by frozen version and scenario"><table><caption>Result criterion ratings, with each scenario kept separate</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Case, condition and version</th><th scope="col">Scenario</th>{study.rubric.result.map((criterion, index) => <th scope="col" title={criterion.description}>{resultLabels[index]}<small>{axes[criterion.axis]}</small></th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(row => <tr><th scope="row">{shortCase(row.run)} · {row.run.condition}<small>{row.stage} · v{row.version.artifact_version}</small></th><td>{row.scenario.difficulty}</td>{study.rubric.result.map(criterion => <td>{score(row.review, criterion.id)}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <details class="disclosure"><summary>Rating anchors</summary><dl>{Object.entries(study.rubric.anchors).map(([value, description]) => <div><dt><strong>{value === 'unknown' ? 'Unknown' : value}</strong></dt><dd>{description}</dd></div>)}</dl></details>
  </details>
  <p><strong>User-requested update:</strong> {updates.length ? 'A new frozen version is retained separately above. Its new feature, repeated scenario tests and expert reviews can be traced in the handoff specialist conversation.' : 'Pending. The handoff team will respond to a request for a copyable practice summary, preserve its earlier version, and repeat the scenario tests and expert reviews.'}</p>
  <p class="muted">The run records identify the manual response transport and retained model output. Expertise boundaries are role instructions; they do not erase a model’s prior knowledge. This small pilot illustrates a workflow and exposes questions to test with people.</p>
  <p><a href="/agentic-le/dynamic/study/overview.json">Download this evidence summary</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/blob/main/docs/lifecycle/dynamic-flower-study.md">Read the protocol and recorded method amendments</a></p>
</section>
<style>
  .evidence-scroll{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0}.evidence-scroll:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent-2);outline-offset:3px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5}caption{text-align:left;font-weight:650;padding:.4rem 0 .8rem}th,td{padding:.7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;vertical-align:top;min-width:5rem}thead th{background:var(--tint);font-weight:700}tbody th{min-width:14rem;font-weight:600}small{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:400;margin-top:.25rem}.update-scores>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 5rem;gap:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.5rem 0}.update-scores dd{margin:0}p{max-width:none}.disclosure{margin:1rem 0}.pilot-evidence{scroll-margin-top:6rem}
</style>
